{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-19:g3_proxy:1","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"lost-precise-model-error-location","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":410,"end_line":412},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":435,"end_line":451},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":638,"end_line":645},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":970,"end_line":974}],"mechanism_tags":["cross_file_contract","unstable_token"],"rationale":"with_origin unconditionally replaces an inner expression-level origin, even when the replacement is None or less precise. State and struct type resolution then retain only the enclosing declaration span, while Display ignores ModelError::span entirely when origin is absent, so public build/parse callers can lose the actionable location of nested constant-expression errors.","severity":"medium"},{"local_id":"shadowed-forall-binder-bypasses-write-check","locations":[{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":1349,"end_line":1359},{"path":"rust/fsl-core/src/model.rs","start_line":1375,"end_line":1381}],"mechanism_tags":["check_write_gap","repeated_effect","repeatable_entry","unstable_scope_key"],"rationale":"The forall write check identifies binders only by their textual name. With nested loops that shadow the same name, a write such as m[i] is judged injective for both binders even though the index refers to the inner binder; every outer iteration can therefore repeat writes to all of the same locations without triggering the action's at-most-once validation.","severity":"high"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:2078bfc5c3b40d3ee1145f6669af7132b7827580e66c8371d00971ab7276ab36","disposition":"not_applicable","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"benchmark-context:sha256:48cbfa2fdedc9d1df47e6b70f785444b81390403df62f5c6c3edaaf776d4f3f2","disposition":"not_applicable","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet